    "durationMs": 206930,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully validated — 32/32 checks pass when run through `sh start.sh` exactly as the harness will invoke it.\n\n**Implementation** (ASP.NET Core 8 / EF Core 8 + Npgsql):\n- `Controllers/LinksController.cs` — all four endpoints: `POST /links` (201 with generated 8-char code or custom code, 409 on duplicate, 422 on validation failure), `GET /links` (ascending creation order with `total`), `GET /links/{code}` (200/404), `GET /r/{code}` (302 + atomic `ExecuteUpdate` click increment, exactly once per request)\n- `Program.cs` — custom `InvalidModelStateResponseFactory` so malformed JSON, missing/invalid url, and invalid codes all return **422** with an `error` field; pending migrations applied at startup\n- `Data/DatabaseUrl.cs` — parses the `DATABASE_URL` PostgreSQL URL into an Npgsql connection string (nothing hard-coded)\n- `Migrations/InitialCreate` — `Links` table with unique `Code` index; collision-safe retry loop for generated codes\n- `start.sh` — applies migrations (via app startup) then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; README documents startup\n\n**Verified**: every status code and response shape in the spec, URL returned unchanged, click count surviving a server restart (data persisted in Postgres), and idempotent migration re-runs. Test servers are stopped and the table truncated, so the environment is clean for the real test suite."
  }
